737	 * Description:
738	 *   Enqueue the audio buffer in the downstream device.  Normally we are
739	 *   called with a buffer of data to be enqueued in the audio stream.
740	 *
741	 *   Be we may also receive an empty length buffer (with only the
742	 *   AUDIO_APB_FINAL set) in the event of certain read error occurs or in the
743	 *   event that the file was an exact multiple of the nmaxbytes size of the
